<title>USA: Tandy Q1 oper shr $0.60 vs $0.48.</title>
<headline>Tandy Q1 oper shr $0.60 vs $0.48.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>TANDY CORPORATION AND SUBSIDIARIES</p>
<p>Consolidated Statements of Income (Unaudited)</p>
<p>(in millions, except per share amounts)</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>							   March 31,</p>
<p>								1997     1996</p>
<p> Net sales and operating revenues	     $1,291.7 $1,447.0</p>
<p> Cost of products sold				 840.1    955.3</p>
<p> Gross profit					    451.6    491.7</p>
<p> Income before interest and income taxes	  48.5     26.4</p>
<p> Interest income					   2.2	3.8</p>
<p> Interest expense					(9.0)    (7.1)</p>
<p>  Total						    (8.8)    (3.3)</p>
<p> Income before income taxes			   41.7     23.1</p>
<p> Provision for income taxes			   16.1	8.6</p>
<p> Net income						 25.6     14.5</p>
<p> Preferred dividends				     1.6	1.6</p>
<p> Net income available to common shareholders    24.0     12.9</p>
<p>Net income available per average common</p>
<p>  and common equivalent share			 0.43     0.21</p>
<p>Average common and common equivalent</p>
<p>  shares outstanding				    56.3     61.4</p>
<p> Dividends declared per common share		0.20     0.20</p>
<p>NOTE: March 1997 quarter earnings on an 'on-going' store basis were $0.60 a share compared to $0.48 per share last year.</p>
<p>For the quarter ended March 31, 1997 reported net income per average common share was $0.43 after deducting $0.17 per share associated with the cost of exiting Incredible Universe compared to net income per average common share of $0.21 reported last year after the deduction of $0.27 per share associated with the adoption of FASB 121.</p>
</text>
